  "worked_solution": "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $A.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $A$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-2,$ so we move $2$ units to the *left*, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $A$ has a $y$-coordinate of $3,$ so we move $3$ units *up*, in the *positive* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14162111/assets/4ba1b8ea826f2d1a095982b03b58c4e75c711dbad168493a6a0d784064e06a74.png)",
